**RepriceService**:

```php
final class RepriceService
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly EntityManagerInterface $em,
        private readonly DirectoryPersister $persister,
        private readonly CostCalculator $calculator,
    ) {}

    public function reprice(PriceDoc $doc): RepriceResult
    {
        return $this->em->wrapInTransaction(function () use ($doc): RepriceResult {
            $applied = $this->persister->apply($doc);
            $rows = $applied['rows'];
            if ($rows === []) {
                return new RepriceResult(0, Decimal::zero());
            }

            $rowIds = array_map(static fn (PriceRow $r): int => (int)$r->getId(), $rows);
            $con = $this->em->getConnection();
            $placeholders = implode(',', array_fill(0, count($rowIds), '?'));
            /** @var list<int|string> $ids */
            $ids = $con->fetchFirstColumn(
                'SELECT id FROM usage_events WHERE status = ? AND price_row_id IN (' . $placeholders . ')',
                array_merge([EventStatus::Rated->value], $rowIds),
            );

            $delta = Decimal::zero();
            foreach ($ids as $id) {
                /** @var UsageEvent|null $event */
                $event = $this->em->find(UsageEvent::class, (int)$id);
                if ($event === null) continue;
                $row = $event->getPriceRow();
                if ($row === null) continue;
                $old = Decimal::of((string)$event->getCost());
                $new = $this->calculator->priceCost($row, $event->tokenUsage(), $event->getProvider()->offPeak())->roundHalfUp(6);
                $event->setCost($new);
                $this->em->persist(new PriceCorrection($event, $row, $old, $new));
                $delta = $delta->add($new->sub($old));
            }
            $this->em->flush();

            return new RepriceResult(count($ids), $delta->roundHalfUp(6));
        });
    }
}
```

Note: `$event->getProvider()` — lazy-loaded; inside the transaction; fine (1 query per event with provider not in the identity map — provider is likely already loaded by previous operations; acceptable).

